dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.presentation.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.semio.presentation
start body
framing record

# ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL-REAL-CODECS-RUNTIME-REUSE-EVOLUTION presentation wave: REAL binary pack
# frame, replacing the old `serde_json::to_vec`-in-envelope shortcut
# (`📸️snapshot/🦀️component.rs`'s old `ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with`). `format u8` (real, fixed)
# then `schema_len`/`schema_bytes` (real, varint-length-prefixed UTF-8 — matches `write_str_lp`'s
# own wire exactly, the proven BARE `segment` form per the flow report's UPDATE §7 fix) are
# genuinely, fully described. Past that, `masters`/`layouts`/`slides` are HOMOGENEOUS but
# variable-length repeated records — `slides` additionally embeds a data-carrying tagged `SlideShape`
# union whose `TextBox`/`Table` variants further embed `document::DocBlock` (itself a further
# recursive tagged union) — the `protocol-array-of-records`/`protocol-prim-ref-recursion` gap
# (`repeat`'s own arms are tag-dispatched, not "repeat N times, N from a count field", for an
# untagged homogeneous record; `Prim::Ref` unconditionally errors on a nested/recursive field):
# modeled as one opaque trailing `payload` chain, the same honest boundary every P1-P3 pilot's own
# nested/recursive payload uses. The real Rust `encode_presentation_snapshot_binary`/
# `decode_presentation_snapshot_binary` stays genuinely, fully structured (varint counts, per-field
# length-prefixes, real 8-byte LE `f64`s, a real per-variant tag byte for `SlideShape`/
# `PlaceholderKind`, and REUSES document's own real `enc_block`/`dec_block` TEXT codec — embedded as
# a length-prefixed UTF-8 blob per `DocBlock` — for every `blocks`/`notes` leaf rather than
# reinventing `DocBlock`'s own binary shape) — round-trip tested independently by this facet's own
# tests, only the protocol DESCRIPTION stops at this boundary.
header fixed 1
field format u8

segment schema_len varint
segment schema_bytes Array(u8, Field(schema_len))

chain payload bytes
